A||||6||blazin'||Will an 87 front clip fit on an 84?||||1||
Z||000000||blazin'||11-02-2001||11:11 AM||||I was wondering if you could take the front clip off an 87 coupe and put it on an 84??<P>Just wondering||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-02-2001||12:03 PM||||Yes.  The hood and fenders are the same, so all you really need to change is the front bumper cover.  You will also need the inner fender wells from the '87 coupe so everything lines up properly.  <P>All in all it is a very easy thing to do and should only take a couple of hours.  You will need to remove the hood to gain access to some of the bolts holding the bumper cover on, but that is the hardest part.....the rest is very straight forward. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||11-02-2001||12:12 PM||||Just out of curiousity does the 5mph "egg crate" bumper behind the fascia work for both the '84 and '87 coupe bumpers?  Pretty sure it does but not sure, I know you could make it work with some trimming.||||reg||5
Z||000003||mrfiero||11-02-2001||12:27 PM||||I believe that the are "technically" different, but can be made to work.  I've never seen the two side by side, so I can't say for sure how they are different.  It might be easier to just grab the eggcrate thing from the '87 coupe as well. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Voytek||11-02-2001||01:01 PM||||You will also need the following:<BR>1.  Underside trimmings (the little air dam thing with metal rail) - necessary for proper installation.<P>2.  The marker lights from the '87 - they are different than your '84 and will NOT fit.  You will also notice that the '87 will have the round molding trim and marker lights, while your '84 has the grooved ones.<P>3.  The shock-absorbing plastic (honeycomb) from inside the facia (attached to the frame) - they are different but mount just the same.<P>Someone said inner fender wells - a must.<P>You may not need to remove the hood (possibly just loosen the bolts on the hood and slide it up).  I haven't had to remove mine when I swapped an '87 GT facia to an '85.<P>All in all an easy project.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||blazin'||11-02-2001||01:11 PM||||Great! Thats what I wanted to hear! <BR>I found a junked 87 coupe a few miles outa town and the guy is giving it away! Dirt cheap! Hopefully the necessary parts are in decent shape! Thanks!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||fotofrank||11-02-2001||01:13 PM||||I installed an '87 fascia on my '84. The only thigs I changed where the Fascia and side markers. I didnot take the "hood" off but it would help. I trimmed the crush material to alow the fascia to fit. I dodn't<BR>plan to hit anything. Good luch ( meant to say luck but it's lunch time here in Chicagoland) and contact me if you have any problems.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4 <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fotofrank (edited 11-02-2001).]||||reg||10
